<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Veluvana</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Venuvana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Veluvana, the Bamboo Grove, was a park outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajgir">Rajagriha</a>, the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magadha">Magadha</a>, which King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bimbisara">Bimbisara</a> gave to the Buddha and his order of monks. It is remembered as the first monastery donated to the Buddhist sangha, and the Buddha spent several rainy seasons there. The site, in present-day Rajgir in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>, is still visited by pilgrims.</p></div>
